    "formula_steps": [
      "Use the 120 closes at 09:31-11:30 and the 120 closes at 13:01-15:00; preserve but exclude standalone 09:30.",
      "Require all 240 selected closes to be finite and strictly positive, then form 119 adjacent log returns inside each half-session; do not form the lunch return.",
      "For every trade date and each of the 238 aligned return positions, accumulate the arithmetic sum and valid-stock count across the exact immutable joint-clean stock-day pool.",
      "For stock i at each return position t, subtract r_i,t from the cross-sectional sum and one from the count, then divide to obtain the equal-weight leave-one-out market return m_-i,t.",
      "Require at least 50 leave-one-out peers at every one of the 238 positions.",
      "Across the 238 aligned pairs compute the ordinary intercept-adjusted Pearson correlation rho between the stock vector and its leave-one-out market vector.",
      "Return 1-rho^2. A constant stock vector or constant leave-one-out market vector is missing; otherwise only a 1e-12 floating-point endpoint canonicalization to [0,1] is allowed.",
      "Do not use signed correlation, beta, index or subgroup benchmarks, peer weighting, trimming, winsorization, robust regression, lagging, residual moments, rank transforms, thresholds, clipping, imputation, or another source field."
    ],
    "formula": "1 - Corr(r_i,t, mean(r_j,t for all valid j != i))^2 over the 238 within-half one-minute log returns",
    "validity": {
      "all_240_selected_closes_finite_and_strictly_positive": true,
      "all_238_stock_returns_finite": true,
      "minimum_leave_one_out_peers_at_every_position": 50,
      "ordinary_pearson_with_intercept": true,
      "constant_stock_return_vector_policy": "missing",
      "constant_leave_one_out_market_vector_policy": "missing",
      "allowed_closed_interval": [
        0,
        1
      ],
      "endpoint_canonicalization_tolerance": 1e-12,
      "statistical_clipping_imputation_winsorization_rank_transform_threshold_weight_substitution_or_daily_substitution_allowed": false
    },
    "hypothesis": "A high value means the stock's minute price discovery is less synchronized with the contemporaneous broad market and therefore contains more firm-specific information that may persist from the next open through the third close.",
    "economic_distinction": "The factor is not computable from a single stock-day: changing other stocks' aligned minute returns changes its leave-one-out benchmark and value while leaving the stock's own path fixed. It uses no amount, volume, source open/high/low, daily market state, index price, industry label, market capitalization, or forward return.",
